    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i just updated the A records for a client site but the new IP isnt showing up for me yet. why does it take so long to actually update everywhere?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This delay is due to DNS propagation, which is the time it takes for DNS record changes to update across all of the internet's servers. Different recursive DNS servers worldwide cache old information, so it can take anywhere from a few minutes to 48 hours for the new IP to become visible everywhere. You can use a DNS checker tool online to monitor how far and fast the update has spread.",
