    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i get the caching part, but it's just weird how it's so inconsistent. like sometimes it's totally gone in one region and then it's like the data is just being held back or playing hide and seek with certain ISPs. is there anything we can do to speed up that \"refresh\" cycle or are we just stuck waiting for the TTLs to expire?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The primary mechanism to influence this is by setting low Time-To-Live (TTL) values on your records before making the change. A low TTL tells caching servers to check for updates more frequently, speeding up the transition. However, once a high TTL is in place, it effectively locks in the old data until the timer runs out, so managing TTL carefully before and after updates is crucial.",
      "source": "target",
